## THE TWO UPLOAD TEMPLATES (ground truth)

Both are two-sheet workbooks. Sheet 1 is **Instructions** (guidance only, never data). Sheet 2 is the data sheet.

### OSD template — sheet 2 named `OSD`
```
Row 1:  FORMULATION COMPOSITION  –  OSD (Oral Solid Dosage)      [merged A1:J1, title]
Row 2:  Enter one ingredient per row. Fill only the strengths…   [merged A2:J2, instruction]
Row 3:  (blank)
Row 4:  S. No. | Name of Ingredient | Function | OSD (Oral Solid Dosage) ×3 (merged pairs) | Remarks
Row 5:  (blank ×3)                              | Strength-1 | Strength-2 | Strength-3     |
Row 6:  (blank ×3)                              | Qty / unit dose | Max Daily Dose | …×3   |
Row 7+: data
```
Columns: A=S.No, B=Name, C=Function, **D/E=Strength-1 (Qty per unit / MDD)**, **F/G=Strength-2**, **H/I=Strength-3**, J=Remarks.

### Injectable template — sheet 2 named `Injectable`
```
Row 4:  S. No. | Name of Ingredient | Function | Injectable / Parenteral ×3 (merged triples) | Remarks
Row 5:  (blank ×3)                              | Strength-1 | Strength-2 | Strength-3
Row 6:  (blank ×3)                              | Qty / mL | Qty / unit dose | Max Daily Dose | …×3
Row 7+: data
```
Columns: A=S.No, B=Name, C=Function, **D/E/F=Strength-1 (Qty per mL / Qty per unit / MDD)**, **G/H/I=Strength-2**, **J/K/L=Strength-3**, M=Remarks.

### Critical structural facts you must handle
1. **Strength labels vary.** The blank template ships `Strength-1 / Strength-2 / Strength-3`, but a user may overwrite row 5 with a real value — e.g. `100 mg | 50 mg | 25 mg`. **Both must work.** A user-entered mg value in the band row must be preserved and used; it must never be silently replaced by the ordinal.
2. **Header cells contain line breaks.** The shipped sub-headers are literally `"Qty /\nunit dose"` and `"Max Daily\nDose"`. Any hint/keyword matching must normalise whitespace before comparing, or `"max daily dose"` will never match `"max daily\ndose"`.
3. **Merged cells.** Row-4 group banners span the pair/triple; row-5 strength labels may too. The blank template also merges the DATA columns on every row in some saved copies — a writer or reader that ignores merges will silently lose the second and third columns.
4. **Footnote marks** are declared in Instructions: `*` = salt form (state free-base equivalent), `@` = removed in processing, `q.s.` = quantity sufficient.

